            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for a promotion, then the Hindi for a matter of honour."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: इनाम",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "इनाम — inām — \"a prize, a reward\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अगर तुम दौड़ जीतोगे तो तुम्हें इनाम मिलेगा। agar tum dauṛ jītoge to tumhẽ inām milegā. If you win the race, you'll get a prize."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "इनाम (inām) is usually traced to Arabic inʿām, \"a favour, a gift\", which reached Hindi through Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
